# Git branching

Read `defaultBaseBranch` from `.agent-workflow/project.config.json` (e.g. `main`, `develop`).

## New ticket branch

```bash
git fetch origin --prune
git checkout <defaultBaseBranch>
git pull --ff-only origin <defaultBaseBranch>
git checkout -b PROJ-123
```

Branch name = exact issue key unless the team uses another convention (document in `PROJECT.md`).

## Resume existing branch

```bash
git fetch origin --prune
git checkout PROJ-123
git merge origin/<defaultBaseBranch>
```

Use **merge**, not rebase, on branches already pushed.

## Before every push / PR

```bash
git fetch origin
git merge origin/<defaultBaseBranch>
```

One ticket per branch. Release/hotfix branches need explicit user approval (`proj-no-release-without-approval.mdc`).
